    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Seeds of Love is Tears for Fears’ ambitious third studio album, originally released in 1989. Moving beyond the streamlined synth-pop and arena-rock of Songs from the Big Chair, it blends psychedelic pop, soul, jazz, progressive rock, and Beatlesque studio craft into richly layered arrangements. The album’s expansive centerpiece, “Sowing the Seeds of Love,” pairs orchestral color and baroque detail with an idealistic, politically charged lyric, while “Woman in Chains” and “Advice for the Young at Heart” emphasize the group’s soulful and emotionally direct side. Though its extended production and elaborate construction divided critics, the album reached number one in the UK and became an international success.\n\nThis Mercury reissue presents the original album in a newly prepared stereo mix by Steven Wilson, pressed on striking Sunburst Orange & Red vinyl. Wilson’s mix offers a fresh perspective on the record’s dense instrumentation, vocal harmonies, and carefully sculpted studio textures while preserving the album’s distinctive late-1980s character. As both a bold artistic departure and the culmination of Tears for Fears’ most adventurous period, The Seeds of Love remains a compelling document of pop ambition, musical experimentation, and meticulous production.",
